\header\pard\qr\fs16\cf4 Gomoa West Constituency Digital Platform\par
\footer\pard\qc\fs16\cf4 Confidential proposal \bullet\ 29 October 2026 \bullet\ Page \chpgn\par

\pard\sa220\cf2\f1\fs20 DIGITAL ACCOUNTABILITY \& ENGAGEMENT PLATFORM\par
\pard\sa80\f1\fs56\cf1 Gomoa West\par
\pard\sa240\f1\fs42\cf1 Constituency Portal\par
\pard\sa180\f2\fs25\cf4 A practical proposal to make constituency delivery visible, verifiable, and easier for residents to engage with.\par
\pard\sa240\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\brdrcf3\par
\pard\sa80\f0\fs19\cf4 Prepared for\par
\pard\sa50\f1\fs26\cf1 Hon. Richard Gyan-Mensah\par
\pard\sa220\f0\fs19\cf4 Member of Parliament, Gomoa West\par
\pard\sa120\f0\fs18\cf4 Prepared by: Constituency Digital Platform Team\par
\pard\sa360\f0\fs17\cf4 29 October 2026\par
\pard\sa180\shading10000\cf6\f1\fs20 A resident should be able to see what is planned, what is underway, what has been delivered, and how to participate.\par
\page

\pard\s1 Executive proposition\par
\pard\s3 This proposal adapts the proven structure of the existing Tarkwa Nsuaem public-service portal into a dedicated Gomoa West Constituency Portal. It is not a template website or a campaign microsite. It is a governed, public-facing operating system for communicating delivery, maintaining an evidence-led project record, and receiving structured feedback from residents.\par
\pard\s3 The platform gives the Office of the MP one trusted digital home for project updates, community activity, media, constituency information, and public enquiries. It is designed to complement—not replace—formal government, Assembly, procurement, or parliamentary records.\par
\pard\s2 The decision requested\par
\pard\s3 Approve a 10-day discovery and content-verification sprint, nominate the office owners, and select five pilot projects or programmes. On that basis, the platform can be configured, populated, and launched in a controlled 12-week rollout.\par
\pard\s2 What Gomoa West receives\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab A distinctly Gomoa West branded website for projects, news, events, gallery, impact, and contact.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab A searchable public project archive with community, category, year, status, and budget filters.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Individual project pages with source, funding, milestones, progress, images, updates, documents, and before-and-after evidence where appropriate.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab A protected admin workspace that lets the constituency office publish and correct content without relying on a developer for routine updates.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab A governance rhythm, launch plan, staff training, and a measurable first-90-day adoption scorecard.\par
\pard\s2 The core principle\par
\pard\s3 No Tarkwa Nsuaem project information, figures, names, or images should be presented as Gomoa West content. The existing system supplies the delivery model and interface components; all Gomoa West records must be verified locally before publication.\par
\page

\pard\s1 Why this matters for Gomoa West\par
\pard\s3 Constituency work is often visible in communities but fragmented online: updates may sit across conversations, flyers, photos, WhatsApp groups, and separate social accounts. That makes it difficult for residents to follow a project from commitment through delivery, and it makes routine questions unnecessarily hard for the office to manage.\par
\pard\s3 A single transparent portal improves the experience on both sides. Residents can self-serve for current, factual information; the office can publish once, link everywhere, and retain a structured record of delivery over time.\par
\pard\s2 Outcomes the platform is designed to create\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Trust through clarity: show project stage, last update date, evidence, and the responsible delivery partner where disclosure is appropriate.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Better engagement: make it simple to find office contact channels, town halls, community events, and ways to submit a request.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Stronger office operations: replace scattered information with one editorial workflow and a repeatable update cadence.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Useful evidence for advocacy: aggregate the visible delivery record and resident demand signals into a clearer briefing base for the MP and partners.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab A durable constituency asset: the public record continues beyond individual announcements and is managed by the office, not by a single social-media account.\par
\pard\s2 Positioning\par
\pard\s3 The portal should be introduced as the official digital information and engagement hub of the Office of the MP for Gomoa West. Its tone should be service-led, factual, and non-exclusionary: residents see what is known, what is pending, and how to participate.\par
\page

\pard\s1 The Gomoa West portal: capabilities to adopt\par
\pard\s3 The current platform already contains the functional foundation below. The Gomoa West rollout configures its identity, replaces all demonstration records with verified local content, and sets office routines around it.\par
\pard\s2 1. Public delivery dashboard\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Homepage summary of verified priorities, project status, community reach, and recent activity.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Project archive with filters for community, sector, year, stage, and budget range.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Project profiles covering objective, source/funding, milestone history, delivery evidence, risks, and next action.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Before-and-after media and progress display where a meaningful comparison is available.\par
\pard\s2 2. Communications and participation\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab News and press updates; an events calendar for town halls, outreach, stakeholder meetings, and programmes.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Photo/video/document gallery and downloadable public notices.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Contact and feedback routes with clear service standards and an FAQ section for repeat questions.\par
\pard\s2 3. Managed office operations\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Secure administrator access, content forms, image upload support, category management, and records that can be updated without a code release.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Structured fields that standardise the facts collected for every project and make public pages consistent.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab A publish workflow: draft, verify, approve, publish, review.\par
\pard\s2 Content architecture for launch\par
\pard\s3 Initial navigation: Home | About the MP | Priorities | Projects | News | Events | Gallery | Impact | Contact. Optional additions after discovery include a scholarships/programmes hub, a community directory, frequently requested letters/forms, and a language-access plan.\par
\page

\pard\s1 12-week adoption plan\par
\pard\s2 Phase 1: Discover and govern \emdash\ Weeks 1-2\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Hold a half-day working session with the MP, constituency office, selected Assembly/community representatives, and communications lead.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Agree the portal purpose, priority audiences, top communities/programmes for launch, content rules, approval authority, and escalation path.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Create the verified master inventory: project/programme name, location, status, source, available documents, images, last-confirmed date, and data owner.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Select five pilot records that demonstrate range and have adequate evidence.\par
\pard\s2 Phase 2: Configure and populate \emdash\ Weeks 3-5\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Apply Gomoa West identity, MP biography approved by the office, contact channels, domain, and navigation.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Migrate verified pilot records; create news, event, FAQ, impact, and media content from approved materials.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Configure the project taxonomy and standard update template. Every published project must show its last verification date.\par
\pard\s2 Phase 3: Test and pilot \emdash\ Weeks 6-8\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Train office users through real publishing tasks and provide a concise operations guide.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Run quality checks on mobile usability, links, image consent, factual accuracy, and accessibility.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Invite a small community review group to test whether information is easy to find and understandable.\par
\pard\s2 Phase 4: Launch and embed \emdash\ Weeks 9-12\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Launch with a town-hall demonstration, QR cards/posters, WhatsApp-ready links, and a short explainer video or visual.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Publish the first monthly update and publicise a clear response standard for enquiries.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Review the first usage and content-quality report; refine navigation, FAQs, and the next project batch.\par
\page

\pard\s1 Operating model: make it credible\par
\pard\s3 The technology is the easy part. The value comes from disciplined, named ownership of the information that residents see. The proposal therefore builds the platform and the routine together.\par
\pard\s2 Recommended roles\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Executive sponsor \emdash\ MP: approves direction, public commitments, and sensitive corrections.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Portal owner \emdash\ Constituency office lead: owns the calendar, workflow, and weekly publication readiness.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Data stewards \emdash\ project/programme focal persons: verify status, location, partner/source, evidence, and next milestone.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Communications editor \emdash\ prepares resident-friendly stories, photography, event notices, and social distribution.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Technical administrator \emdash\ manages access, support, backups, and major platform updates.\par
\pard\s2 Minimum publishing standard\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Every project page has a named data owner and a last-verified date.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Ongoing projects are reviewed at least every 14 days; planned, completed, or stalled records are updated when a material decision occurs.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Unconfirmed figures are not published as facts. Where a funding amount or date is unavailable, the portal states that it is pending verification.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Sensitive personal data, private requests, and images without appropriate consent remain off the public site.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab A correction path is visible: residents can flag an inaccuracy, and the office logs and resolves it through the approval workflow.\par
\pard\s2 Engagement rhythm\par
\pard\s3 Weekly: editorial check-in and priority enquiries. Fortnightly: active-project status review. Monthly: public round-up and dashboard update. Quarterly: town hall or community review that uses the portal record as a common reference point.\par
\page

\pard\s1 Success measures and safeguards\par
\pard\s2 First-90-day scorecard\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab 100\'25 of the launch inventory labelled with a data owner and last-verified date.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab At least 85\'25 of the selected priority records supported by a verifiable source, document, or approved field evidence.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab 90\'25 of active-project updates published within the agreed 14-day review window.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab 90\'25 of public enquiries acknowledged within two working days, even where the substantive answer needs longer.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab A baseline of visits, searches, requests, and event clicks established by the end of the first month; targets are then set from actual behaviour rather than guesswork.\par
\pard\s2 Safeguards\par
\pard\s3 Accuracy: use a source and approval check before publication. Privacy: do not expose sensitive casework or children\'s information; obtain appropriate consent for recognisable images. Security: least-privilege admin access and regular access review. Continuity: assign at least two trained editors and retain the verified source record behind each published claim.\par
\pard\s2 What is deliberately out of scope for launch\par
\pard\s3 The first release should not attempt to digitise every constituency record or promise a public answer to every complex case. It prioritises a clean, credible foundation: verified information, the most useful resident journeys, trained office owners, and a dependable update rhythm. Additional services can be added after the pilot is stable.\par
\pard\s2 Implementation prerequisites\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Approved name, visual identity, portrait/biography, and official contact channels.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Five verified pilot project/programme records, associated evidence, and permissions to use media.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Nomination of the portal owner, data stewards, and communications editor.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab A launch date and approval to run the discovery session.\par
\page

\pard\s1 Recommended next steps\par
\pard\s3 The proposed next move is modest and decisive: start with a discovery sprint, use it to settle governance and content quality, then launch a focused pilot that can grow without losing credibility.\par
\pard\s2 Week-one action list\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Confirm sponsorship from the Office of the MP and name the four operating roles.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Schedule the half-day discovery workshop.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Share available project/programme lists, public notices, reports, photos, and event calendars for verification.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Choose five pilot records representing priority areas and different stages of delivery.\par
\pard\s5\bullet\tab Approve the public positioning: Gomoa West\'s official information and engagement hub.\par
\pard\s2 Closing statement\par
\pard\s3 Gomoa West does not need to begin from a blank page. The functional foundation already exists. What will make this adoption successful is a careful localisation process: verified Gomoa West content, clear office ownership, a resident-first launch, and a reliable public record that earns trust over time.\par
\pard\sa220\shading10000\cf6\f1\fs22 Proposed outcome: a trusted digital front door for the Office of the MP and a transparent, living record of constituency delivery.\par
\pard\s2 Reference note\par
\pard\s3 The recipient designation used in this proposal is based on the Parliament of Ghana member record for Hon. Richard Gyan-Mensah, Member of Parliament for Gomoa West, accessed 29 October 2026: parliament.gh/members?mp=94013. All future Gomoa West project, programme, budget, impact, and media content should be verified by the constituency office before publication.\par
